{"schemaVersion":1,"generatedAt":"2026-08-16T16:20:46.501Z","id":"23df2eac3a5a50009a9376c5","canonicalUrl":"https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260727073454.2019759-1-daniel.turull%40ericsson.com/","channels":["openembedded-core"],"thread":{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"thread:lore-git:20260727073454.2019759-1-daniel.turull@ericsson.com","source":{"kind":"static-generated","canonicalThreadUrl":"https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260727073454.2019759-1-daniel.turull%40ericsson.com/","fetchedAt":"2026-08-16T16:20:46.501Z","contentDigest":"lore-git:20260727073454.2019759-1-daniel.turull@ericsson.com"},"subject":"Re: [scarthgap][PATCH] libarchive: fix CVE-2026-14164","messages":{"1ae24cc1f9ab292cbc5bc02068feee6cb7a5d77f.camel@pbarker.dev":{"id":"1ae24cc1f9ab292cbc5bc02068feee6cb7a5d77f.camel@pbarker.dev","messageId":"1ae24cc1f9ab292cbc5bc02068feee6cb7a5d77f.camel@pbarker.dev","references":["20260727073454.2019759-1-daniel.turull@ericsson.com"],"missingAncestorIds":["20260727073454.2019759-1-daniel.turull@ericsson.com"],"author":{"name":"Paul Barker","address":"paul@pbarker.dev"},"replyTo":[],"to":[{"name":"","address":"daniel.turull@ericsson.com"},{"name":"","address":"openembedded-core@lists.openembedded.org"}],"cc":[],"timestamp":{"raw":"2026-08-16T09:35:05.000Z","iso":"2026-08-16T09:35:05.000Z","valid":true},"subject":"Re: [scarthgap][PATCH] libarchive: fix CVE-2026-14164","mailingLists":[{"id":"openembedded-core.lists.openembedded.org","displayName":"openembedded-core.lists.openembedded.org"}],"blocks":[{"kind":"quote","attribution":"On Mon, 2026-07-27 at 09:34 +0200, daniel.turull@ericsson.com wrote:","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":"From: Daniel Turull <daniel.turull@ericsson.com>"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"Backport patch to fix CVE-2026-14164."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"References:"},{"depth":1,"text":"  https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-14164"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"Upstream fix:"},{"depth":1,"text":"  https://github.com/libarchive/libarchive/commit/f774f03b40cb109348e5c6d52b59c864e3cfa8e8"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"Signed-off-by: Daniel Turull <daniel.turull@ericsson.com>"},{"depth":1,"text":"---"},{"depth":1,"text":" .../libarchive/CVE-2026-14164.patch           | 52 +++++++++++++++++++"},{"depth":1,"text":" .../libarchive/libarchive_3.7.9.bb            |  1 +"},{"depth":1,"text":" 2 files changed, 53 insertions(+)"},{"depth":1,"text":" create mode 100644 meta/recipes-extended/libarchive/libarchive/CVE-2026-14164.patch"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"diff --git a/meta/recipes-extended/libarchive/libarchive/CVE-2026-14164.patch b/meta/recipes-extended/libarchive/libarchive/CVE-2026-14164.patch"},{"depth":1,"text":"new file mode 100644"},{"depth":1,"text":"index 00000000000..c94764acf29"},{"depth":1,"text":"--- /dev/null"},{"depth":1,"text":"+++ b/meta/recipes-extended/libarchive/libarchive/CVE-2026-14164.patch"},{"depth":1,"text":"@@ -0,0 +1,52 @@"},{"depth":1,"text":"+From 5efdd23ea2569314d62492bdc0b078f4dad1f75a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001"},{"depth":1,"text":"+From: \"Dustin L. Howett\" <dustin@howett.net>"},{"depth":1,"text":"+Date: Sun, 24 May 2026 12:43:00 -0500"},{"depth":1,"text":"+Subject: [PATCH] Merge pull request #3071 from stoeckmann/rar5_doublefree"},{"depth":1,"text":"+"},{"depth":1,"text":"+rar5: Avoid dangling pointers in init_unpack"},{"depth":1,"text":"+(cherry picked from commit 42453cf16255800726b4efedab25138639ceef20)"},{"depth":1,"text":"+"},{"depth":1,"text":"+Conflicts Resolved:"},{"depth":1,"text":"+"},{"depth":1,"text":"+libarchive/archive_read_support_format_rar5.c (1 conflict):"},{"depth":1,"text":"+- Stable's init_unpack() is a void function without the calloc failure"},{"depth":1,"text":"+  checks (`if(...== NULL) return ARCHIVE_FATAL;`) that exist upstream,"},{"depth":1,"text":"+  since it predates that hardening. Kept the CVE fix logic (unconditionally"},{"depth":1,"text":"+  setting rar->cstate.window_buf and rar->cstate.filtered_buf to NULL right"},{"depth":1,"text":"+  after free(), and removing the redundant else-branch that only NULLed"},{"depth":1,"text":"+  them when window_size <= 0) and omitted the ARCHIVE_FATAL return checks,"},{"depth":1,"text":"+  which don't apply to this void-returning stable version."},{"depth":1,"text":"+"},{"depth":1,"text":"+Assisted-by: kiro:claude-sonnet-5"},{"depth":1,"text":"+"},{"depth":1,"text":"+Changes from upstream commit f774f03b40cb:"},{"depth":1,"text":"+  - libarchive/archive_read_support_format_rar5.c: adapted from upstream"},{"depth":1,"text":"+"},{"depth":1,"text":"+CVE: CVE-2026-14164"},{"depth":1,"text":"+Upstream-Status: Backport [https://github.com/libarchive/libarchive/commit/f774f03b40cb109348e5c6d52b59c864e3cfa8e8]"},{"depth":1,"text":"+"},{"depth":1,"text":"+Signed-off-by: Daniel Turull <daniel.turull@ericsson.com>"},{"depth":1,"text":"+---"},{"depth":1,"text":"+ libarchive/archive_read_support_format_rar5.c | 6 +++---"},{"depth":1,"text":"+ 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)"},{"depth":1,"text":"+"},{"depth":1,"text":"+diff --git a/libarchive/archive_read_support_format_rar5.c b/libarchive/archive_read_support_format_rar5.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"+index 736c95a6..098cd6f7 100644"},{"depth":1,"text":"+--- a/libarchive/archive_read_support_format_rar5.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"++++ b/libarchive/archive_read_support_format_rar5.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"+@@ -2489,12 +2489,12 @@ static void init_unpack(struct rar5* rar) {"},{"depth":1,"text":"+ \tfree(rar->cstate.window_buf);"},{"depth":1,"text":"+ \tfree(rar->cstate.filtered_buf);"},{"depth":1,"text":"+ "},{"depth":1,"text":"++\trar->cstate.window_buf = NULL;"},{"depth":1,"text":"++\trar->cstate.filtered_buf = NULL;"},{"depth":1,"text":"++"},{"depth":1,"text":"+ \tif(rar->cstate.window_size > 0) {"},{"depth":1,"text":"+ \t\trar->cstate.window_buf = calloc(1, rar->cstate.window_size);"},{"depth":1,"text":"+ \t\trar->cstate.filtered_buf = calloc(1, rar->cstate.window_size);"},{"depth":1,"text":"+-\t} else {"},{"depth":1,"text":"+-\t\trar->cstate.window_buf = NULL;"},{"depth":1,"text":"+-\t\trar->cstate.filtered_buf = NULL;"},{"depth":1,"text":"+ \t}"},{"depth":1,"text":"+ "},{"depth":1,"text":"+ \tclear_data_ready_stack(rar);"}],"lineCount":75,"maximumDepth":1},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Same comment here as I made on the wrynose patch [1]."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"[1]: https://lore.kernel.org/openembedded-core/0447ebc9d29b0736de8ba0c75f155ed4f880d072.camel@pbarker.dev/"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"The `return ARCHIVE_FATAL` paths are not present in libarchive 3.7.9, so\nthe function can't return between while rar->cstate.filtered_buf is\nstill a dangling pointer."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Best regards,"},{"kind":"signature","text":"Paul Barker","lineCount":1}],"patchIds":[],"attachmentMetadata":[],"sourceOrdinal":0,"diagnostics":[],"declaredParentMessageId":"20260727073454.2019759-1-daniel.turull@ericsson.com"}},"rootIds":["1ae24cc1f9ab292cbc5bc02068feee6cb7a5d77f.camel@pbarker.dev"],"childrenByParent":{},"chronologicalIds":["1ae24cc1f9ab292cbc5bc02068feee6cb7a5d77f.camel@pbarker.dev"],"patchSeries":[],"diagnostics":[],"patches":{}}}